[FEN "r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/2b1p3/2B1P3/3P1N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 5"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ Castling is a king move with strict conditions. Clear squares are necessary, but the king also needs a safe starting square, transit square and destination. } 5. O-O d6 6. c3 { Illustrative line. O-O moves the white king from e1 to g1 and the rook from h1 to f1. White improves king shelter and brings the rook nearer the center in one move. The sample continuation ...d6 c3 supports a future central plan. Before playing it in a game, inspect Black's reply. Castling has improved safety, but it has not removed the need to check threats on every turn. } *

