{ Exercise. Try the questions in the book before reading this line. } 5. Bd2 Nf6 6. Nf3 { Illustrative line. No. The diagonal is d2-c3-b4-a5, and the bishop's line stops at c3. Black is not forced to move the queen in response to Bd2. White's own knight stands on c3. Bishops cannot attack through friendly pieces. Calling this an attack on the queen would miscount the tempo. Yes. Bd2 develops the bishop and can prepare future ideas if the knight moves. In the sample ...Nf6 Nf3, both sides continue development. A useful quiet move does not need to be described as a forcing move to justify it. } *
